.TH CROM 1 "2026-07-30" "crom 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
crom \- find files by name or content, in parallel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crom
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIpattern\fR] [\fIpath\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B crom
walks one or more directory trees and prints the paths that match. A file
matches when its name matches the pattern and, if
.B \-c
is given, its contents contain the given text.
.PP
With no path, the current directory is searched. With no pattern, every file
matches. Paths beginning with
.B \-
must come after
.BR \-\- .
.SS Patterns
A pattern without
.BR * ", " ? " or " [
matches any name that
.I contains
it. A pattern with any of those characters is a glob matched against the
.I whole
name.
.B \-g
forces the whole-name reading for a plain word.
.PP
Case folding follows the pattern: the match ignores case until the pattern
itself contains a capital letter, so
.B crom pdf
finds
.I notes.PDF
but
.B crom PDF
does not. This applies to
.B \-c
as well.
.SS Skipped by default
Dot files and directories, everything excluded by a
.I .gitignore
in scope, and a built-in list of directories
.RI ( .git ", " node_modules ", " __pycache__ ", " build ,
and similar). See
.BR \-H ", " \-\-no\-ignore " and " \-u .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " \fIpattern\fR"
Filename pattern, as if given positionally.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-glob " \fIpattern\fR"
Match the whole name rather than a part of it.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ignore\-case
Fold case in names and in content.
.TP
.B \-\-case\-sensitive
Match exactly as typed.
.TP
.BR \-E ", " \-\-exclude " \fIglob\fR"
Skip entries whose name matches \fIglob\fR. Directories are pruned, not walked.
May be given up to 32 times.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-content " \fItext\fR"
Only report files whose contents contain \fItext\fR. Binary files are skipped
unless
.B \-a
is given.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-type " \fIf\fR|\fId\fR|\fIl\fR"
Report only regular files, directories or symlinks. The default is regular
files.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-size " [+|\-]\fIN\fR"
Only files larger (+) or smaller (\-) than \fIN\fR bytes. Suffixes
.IR k ", " m ", " g
multiply by 1024, 1048576 and 1073741824.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-hidden
Descend into and report dot files and directories.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-unrestricted
Shorthand for
.B \-\-hidden \-\-no\-ignore .
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-follow
Follow symlinks to directories. A directory already on the current path is not
entered again, so cycles terminate.
.TP
.BI \-\-depth " N"
Do not descend more than \fIN\fR levels below each search path.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-results " N"
Stop the search once \fIN\fR matches have been printed.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-exec " \fIcommand\fR"
Run \fIcommand\fR with
.B {}
replaced by each match. The path is passed single-quoted, so shell
metacharacters in file names are inert. A command that would exceed the path
buffer is not run.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " \fIN\fR"
Worker threads. Defaults to the number of usable cores.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-text
Search binary files too.
.TP
.BR \-0 ", " \-\-null
Terminate each result with NUL instead of a newline, for
.BR "xargs \-0" .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one JSON object per result.
.TP
.B \-\-bar
Show a progress bar on stderr once the search passes 250 ms.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-no\-bar
Never show the bar.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ignore
Do not read
.I .gitignore
files.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-messages
Do not report paths that could not be opened.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Do not read
.IR ~/.cromrc .
.TP
.BI \-\-color " when"
.IR auto ", " always " or " never .
.I auto
colours only a terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the option list.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Something matched.
.TP
.B 1
Nothing matched.
.TP
.B 2
A named search path could not be opened, an option was not understood, or the
results are incomplete.
.PP
Directories that could not be read during the walk are reported on stderr but do
not change the exit status.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cromrc
Default options, one or more per line.
.B #
begins a comment.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B crom pdf
Every name containing "pdf", in the current tree.
.TP
.B crom '*.rs' src tests
Rust files under two directories.
.TP
.B crom \-c TODO \-n '*.py'
Python files that mention TODO.
.TP
.B crom \-0 '*.tmp' | xargs \-0 rm
Delete matches safely, whatever the names contain.
.TP
.B crom \-\-max\-results 1 config.toml /
The first config.toml on the system, without walking the rest.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Linux on x86\-64 only. Paths longer than 4096 bytes are skipped and reported.
Patterns are globs, not regular expressions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR find (1),
.BR grep (1),
.BR fd (1),
.BR rg (1)
